WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.989
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will plan coverage and keep

00:00:04.989 --> 00:00:09.979
dispatch aligned. A paper duty schedule and a dispatch roster can drift apart,

00:00:09.979 --> 00:00:14.968
especially when members sign up or trade shifts. We will explain the features,

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:19.190
the setup decisions, and a practical way to check the result.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:24.723
A career department sets up A, B and C shifts, and a volunteer

00:00:24.723 --> 00:00:29.656
department uses shift sign-ups for weekend duty crews. Shifts show who is on

00:00:29.656 --> 00:00:34.589
duty and can drive dispatch, so calls page the people who are actually

00:00:34.589 --> 00:00:39.522
working. The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

00:00:39.522 --> 00:00:41.040
scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:48.114
Shifts. Shift schedules, sign-ups and trades. Create your shifts, assign groups and members,

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:54.588
and decide whether dispatch follows shifts. Availability also depends on Shifts. Check access

00:00:54.588 --> 00:00:56.580
in the target department.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:03.362
Calendar. The department calendar for meetings, events and training nights. Add recurring meetings

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:09.544
and training nights. Availability also depends on Calendar. Check access in the target

00:01:09.544 --> 00:01:10.020
department.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:16.199
New Calendar Event. Add an event to the department calendar. Have your rotation

00:01:16.199 --> 00:01:21.777
or duty schedule, and decide whether dispatch should follow shifts. Availability also depends

00:01:21.777 --> 00:01:25.210
on Calendar. Check access in the target department.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:31.864
Workshifts. Repeating work schedules for staff. Have your rotation or duty schedule, and

00:01:31.864 --> 00:01:37.917
decide whether dispatch should follow shifts. Availability also depends on Shifts. Check access

00:01:37.917 --> 00:01:39.780
in the target department.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:45.445
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Create an assigned

00:01:45.445 --> 00:01:50.509
or signup shift with groups and staffing needs. Step 2. Have demo members

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:55.574
sign up or complete a trade where supported. Step 3. Review whether dispatch

00:01:55.574 --> 00:01:59.470
follows groups or shifts and confirm the calendar time zone.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:05.257
Now verify the result. Compare the scheduled roster with the people dispatch would

00:02:05.257 --> 00:02:10.444
include at the selected time. Check trade completion and the visible duty coverage.

00:02:10.444 --> 00:02:15.631
A common problem to watch for: A calendar event is not automatically a

00:02:15.631 --> 00:02:20.020
duty assignment. Shift dispatch behavior must be reviewed on Dispatch Settings.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:25.953
Your practice task is simple. Schedule a weekend duty crew, change one assignment,

00:02:25.953 --> 00:02:31.285
and verify the expected roster. Track unfilled slots and unresolved trades. Record the

00:02:31.285 --> 00:02:36.618
result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed. Use the

00:02:36.618 --> 00:02:40.310
linked feature scripts for the detailed screen recording plan.

